        "original_id": "27b51a71-2715-58c2-84e6-e92b303843fa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Christian Friedrich Schönbein, William Robert Grove, Robert Cumming\n- Roles: chemists, judges, physical scientists\n- Products: fuel cells, guncotton, ozone\n- Concepts: conservation of energy\n\nFacts:\n- Christian Friedrich Schönbein was a German-Swiss chemist who lived from 18 October 1799 to 29 August 1868.\n- In 1838, Christian Friedrich Schönbein invented the fuel cell at the same time as William Robert Grove and Robert Cumming.\n- Christian Friedrich Schönbein was also known for his discoveries of guncotton and ozone.\n- William Robert Grove was a Welsh judge and physical scientist who lived from 11 July 1811 to 1 August 1896.\n- William Robert Grove anticipated the general theory of the conservation of energy.\n- William Robert Grove was a pioneer of fuel cell technology.",
